eparate node held at its prior, so the cooperate-or-defect payoffs for each choice come out the same whatever the probability r is. Submitting therefore dominates, and the copies end up defecting in the fixed point. The essay's partial-similarity model could soften this, but the strict reading says submit.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working out the decision under A-FDT for two copies that see different observations. Each copy's intervention acts only on its own node, while the other copy's node stays at its prior. In the prisoner's dilemma, I hold the other copy's cooperation probability at r and compare the expected years of quiet against submitting.\n\nUnder strict A-FDT, the other copy's node is a separate node held at its prior, so the cooperate-or-defect payoffs for each choice come out the same whatever the probability r is. Submitting therefore dominates, and the copies end up defecting in the fixed point. The essay's partial-similarity model could soften this, but the strict reading says submit.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9695,"completion_tokens":809,"total_tokens":10504,"cost":0.05496,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05496,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03878,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01618},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":353,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}